    "intro_html":  "Calabacitas means little squashes, and in New Mexico and northern Mexico it means zucchini cooked down with corn, tomato, and chile until everything melts together. It is late-summer garden food, built for the weeks when zucchini is practically free. Add ground turkey and black beans and serve it over rice and you have a full dinner. Each serving runs {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
